<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-ANZ half-year net profit A$615 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-ANZ half-year net profit A$615 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to March 31.</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net			    615 vs  520</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)	    22 vs   18</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name Australia and New Zealand Banking Group Ltd     Operating profit		   949 vs 790</p>
<p>    Total assets (billion)	135.09 vs 119.85</p>
<p>    Interest income (billion)     4.72 vs 4.58</p>
<p>    Interest expense (billion)    3.03 vs 2.93</p>
<p>    Bad debts expense		   75 vs 102</p>
<p>    Other income (billion)	  1.14 vs 1.01</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		 loss 31 vs  nil</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			 41.4 vs 35.80</p>
<p>    Tax				    299 vs 265</p>
<p>    Minorities			     4 vs   5</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date July 7</p>
<p>Reg date June 16</p>
<p>NOTE: ANZ said the abnormal loss reflected restructuring costs and income tax expense on interest earned on its National Housing Bank deposit in India.</p>
<p>Regional operating profit after tax before abnormals</p>
<p>    Australia			  405 vs 301</p>
<p>    New Zealand			 77 vs  68</p>
<p>    UK and Europe		     51 vs  39</p>
<p>    Asia Pacific			42 vs  53</p>
<p>    South Asia			  29 vs  24</p>
<p>    Americas			    12 vs  14</p>
<p>    Middle East			 30 vs  21</p>
<p>NOTE: Operating profit after tax by industry segment:</p>
<p>    General and investment banking    521 vs 418</p>
<p>    Finance				    77 vs  64</p>
<p>    Insurance and funds management     48 vs  38</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
